  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "W3C DID Core is the World Wide Web Consortium Recommendation (published July 2022) defining Decentralised Identifiers (DIDs) \u2014 globally unique, controller-owned URIs of the form did:<method>:<method-specific-id> that are cryptographically verifiable and resolvable without a centralised registration authority. Each DID resolves to a JSON-LD DID Document containing verification methods (public keys), authentication suites, and service endpoints. The specification is method-agnostic, accommodating distributed ledgers, peer-to-peer networks, and web servers as verifiable data registries, and forms the identity layer of the broader Self-Sovereign Identity and Verifiable Credentials ecosystem.",
